            <div xml:id="d1093">

                <pb facs="1004" n="992" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg992"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760d.61/407: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-04T17:00:00+03:00">November 4, 1939—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 4—11:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>863. For the President, Secretary and Under Secretary. I have been informed that
                    on November 2 the Swedish Minister having failed to obtain an appointment with
                    Molotov left a note at the <pb facs="1005" n="993" xml:id="pg993"/> Foreign
                    Office dealing with the Soviet-Finnish negotiations. At about 5 o’clock in the
                    afternoon Molotov sent for the Swedish Minister and handed back the note with
                    the statement that the Soviet-Finnish negotiations were not a matter of concern
                    to Sweden. Obvously, therefore, the outburst against Sweden and the Swedish
                    Foreign Minister, contained in the editorial in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pravda</hi> (see my telegram No. 856, November 3, 3 p.m.), was provoked by
                    these renewed Swedish representations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
